    <div class="beep-play">
      <p class="beep-param-note">Middle row <span dir="ltr"><kbd>A</kbd> … <kbd>'</kbd></span> for the white keys, the row above <span dir="ltr"><kbd>W</kbd> <kbd>E</kbd> <kbd>T</kbd> <kbd>Y</kbd> <kbd>U</kbd> <kbd>O</kbd> <kbd>P</kbd></span> for the black keys, and <kbd>Z</kbd> / <kbd>X</kbd> to shift the octave. It also works with a keyboard plugged into your phone, or by touching the keys directly. Recording shortcuts: <kbd>R</kbd> start/stop, and <kbd>Space</kbd> play/stop after your first recording (the full list appears with it).</p>
      <div class="instrument-picker" id="beepPlayLabels" role="group" aria-label="What is written on the keys">
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip active" data-labels="keys">⌨️ Keyboard letters</button>
