        </div>
        <div class="beep-timeline" id="beepTimeline">
          <div class="beep-ruler" id="beepRuler" title="Ruler: click to set the split point"></div>
          <div class="beep-board" id="beepBoard"></div>
          <div class="beep-playhead" id="beepPlayhead" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <p class="beep-param-note" id="beepTimelineHint">↔️↕️ Drag any layer freely: left and right in time, up and down between tracks (drop it below the last track to start a new one). Drag a layer's left or right edge to shorten or lengthen it without cutting: nothing is deleted, and lengthening brings the hidden notes back. To place the white line, click or drag on the ruler or any empty space, or grab the circle at its top; then select a layer and press Split to cut it there. The Delete key removes it, the arrow keys move it, and a double-click sends it back to the start. All layers play together whichever track they're on.</p>
        <details class="beep-shortcuts" id="beepShortcuts">
          <summary>⌨️ Keyboard shortcuts <span dir="ltr">(Ctrl+/)</span></summary>
          <ul class="beep-shortcut-list">
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Space</kbd></span><span>Play from the white line / stop</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd></span><span>Play from the start</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>R</kbd></span><span>Start / stop recording</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Esc</kbd></span><span>Stop everything and deselect (back to playing with letters)</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Enter</kbd> · <kbd>Home</kbd> · <kbd>End</kbd></span><span>Move the white line to the start · start · end</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>← →</kbd></span><span>Move the focused layer (or the white line if no layer is focused); Shift = one second; ↑ ↓ between tracks</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>S</kbd></span><span>Split the selected layer at the white line — only while a layer is selected; otherwise S plays a piano note</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Delete</kbd> · <kbd>Backspace</kbd></span><span>Delete the layer</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>C</kbd> · <kbd>X</kbd> · <kbd>V</kbd></span><span>Copy · cut · paste at the white line</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>D</kbd></span><span>Duplicate the layer</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>M</kbd></span><span>Mute / unmute the layer</span></li>
            <li><span class="beep-key-combo" dir="ltr"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd> · <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd></span><span>Undo · redo</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="beep-param-note">On a Mac use ⌘ instead of Ctrl. The other piano keys (A…' W…P Z X) stay for playing.</p>
        </details>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="beepRecPlay" data-play="▶️ Play layers" data-stop="⏹ Stop">▶️ Play layers</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="beepRecWav" data-working="⏳ Preparing…" data-failed="Couldn't prepare the file">⬇️ WAV</button>
        <button type="button" class="filter-chip" id="beepRecMp3" data-working="⏳ Preparing…" data-failed="Couldn't prepare the file">⬇️ MP3</button>
